===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|fantasy}} The [[unique]] name of an [[entity]], which can be used to [[control]] or [[manipulate]] that entity.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1968|author=Ursula Le Guin|title=A Wizard of Earthsea|page=59|passage=He saw that in this dusty and fathomless matter of learning the '''true name''' of each place, thing, and being, the power he wanted lay like a jewel at the bottom of a dry well. For magic consists in this, the true naming of a thing.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1987|author=Terry Pratchett|title=Mort|isbn=0061020680|page=229|passage=It would be back to the stone floors and getting up when it was still dark and no alcohol under any circumstances and memorising the '''true names''' of everything until the brain squeaked.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 23 1991|author=Martin Cropper|title=In The Native State|work=The Times|passage=They conjured a world of primitive magic in which evil spirits could not be given their '''true names''' for fear of increasing their power.}}
# {{lb|en|LGBT}} A [[person]]'s preferred name, particularly where this does not match their [[legal name]].
#: {{coordinate terms|en|dead name}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2020-09-29|author=Heidi Neumark|title=Sanctuary: Being Christian in the Wake of Trump|publisher=Wm. B. Eerdmans Publishing|isbn=9781467460002|page=13|text=I suggested to Sofie that another baptism wasn't necessary since God always knew her deepest self, but we could do an affirmation of baptism with her '''true name'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2022-05-06|author=Tom Altstiel|author2=Jean Grow|author3=Dan Augustine|author4=Joanna L. Jenkins|title=Advertising Creative: Strategy, Copy, and Design|publisher=SAGE Publications|isbn=9781071846636|text=Mastercard created the '''True Name''' card - the first payments product feature that allows people to prominently feature the name they associate with on the front of their card, without requiring a legal name change.}}

